  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "funnel_statistics: Fix menu nesting for register_packet_menu()",
  "description": "Previously, multiple menus with the same protocol were grouped\nas a single entry. For example, http/foo1 and http/foo2 would\nboth be under a single \"http\" menu with two entries.\nThe recently-noticed bug was that the two entries were\ncreating two \"http\" menu entries.\n\nThis bug was caused by passing `menuTextToMenus` by value\ninstead of by reference, so the inner function call was\noperating on a copy of `menuTextToMenus`. As such,\neach call to `FunnelAction::addToMenu` was modifying a\nnew object.",
